ALVA — Complete Controller Customization and Beginner-First Recommended Controls Redesign

Mission

Perform a comprehensive redesign and improvement of ALVA’s controller controls, with two primary objectives:

1. Give players complete freedom to customize their controller inputs, including full right-joystick customization and all physically supported controller buttons.
2. Completely reevaluate and redesign the recommended controller layouts for every playable fighter, making them exceptionally natural, intuitive, comfortable, and accessible to new and casual players.

The central design philosophy is:

ALVA’s controller controls should feel so natural that someone playing the game for the first time can intuitively understand how to perform a move by observing what that move actually does.

The player should not have to memorize arbitrary input combinations, struggle with uncomfortable finger movements, or understand the game’s internal attack numbering to enjoy playing.

Our ambition is not merely to make the controller layouts usable. We want them to feel exceptionally well designed, fluid, effortless, and satisfying.

IMPORTANT: You, the implementing agent, must independently determine every recommended controller binding. This task deliberately does not prescribe any specific controller button or joystick direction for any action. Do not treat existing bindings as preferred choices. Investigate the actual game and make your own decisions using the requirements below.

