10. Test the actual player experience

Do not consider this task complete merely because the new configuration passes static validation.

Test controller behavior as a coherent interactive system.

10.1 Joystick customization tests

Verify that:

* Both joysticks can be configured independently.
* The right joystick can activate supported bound actions.
* Left and right joystick directional conditions are distinguished correctly.
* Either joystick can be used as a movement source.
* A joystick not used for movement can still provide independent action inputs.
* Simultaneous joystick inputs behave correctly.
* Returning a stick to neutral releases or resets its directional state appropriately.
* Deadzones prevent accidental activation.
* Press, hold, and continuous actions behave as intended.
* Directional bindings work with supported modifiers.
* Analog input does not produce unintended repeated actions.
* Configuration persists after saving and reloading.

10.2 Complete button customization tests

Verify that every supported physical button can be selected as an input and functions correctly when assigned.

Test appropriate combinations, contextual reuse, conflict detection, input capture, and menu safety.

Verify that remapping a universal action actually changes the gameplay input.

Do not confuse an input being displayed in the editor with an input being successfully supported by the runtime.

10.3 Recommended layout tests

Verify every playable fighter’s recommended profile.

Each fighter must have:

* A complete set of valid bindings.
* No missing playable moves.
* No bindings for nonexistent actions.
* No unresolved conflicts.
* Consistent universal actions.
* Correct ground and aerial behavior.
* A layout genuinely authored around its move mechanics.

Test the newly chosen universal Dash and Defense inputs during actual gameplay.

Test common movement, jumping, attacking, defending, and recovery sequences for physical usability.

10.4 Regression tests

Preserve or appropriately update the existing test coverage for:

* Controller devices and connection management.
* Controller input resolution.
* Controller profiles and conflicts.
* Controller settings and persistence.
* Controller editor UI.
* Controller-based ability HUD.
* Fighter-specific controller expectations.
* Universal movement.
* Dash and air dash.
* Shield and Deflect.
* Combat input buffering.
* Practice Ground fighter switching.
* Pause menus and controller navigation.
* Ground/air action restrictions.
* Focus loss and controller disconnection.
* Localization.

Update tests that explicitly assert obsolete recommended bindings.

Do not weaken tests merely to make a new implementation pass.

Add coverage for new behavior and discovered edge cases.

Run the full repository test suite using node --test and report the results accurately.

Where interactive browser or hardware testing is possible, include it.

