12. Required implementation quality

Prefer a cohesive solution over scattered patches.

The controller system should remain understandable, reusable, and maintainable as ALVA grows.

Avoid hardcoding behavior for individual fighters inside shared input modules.

Avoid duplicating controller-binding logic across the editor, resolver, HUD, and settings.

Use a consistent binding representation and shared utilities where appropriate.

Keep changes focused on controller configuration, input resolution, recommended profiles, and the associated interfaces and tests.

The result should support future fighters and future controller customization improvements without another architectural overhaul.

Do not merely add new configuration options while leaving the input resolver unable to use them.

Do not merely update recommended profile data without reevaluating how those controls feel during real gameplay.

Both objectives—complete player customization and excellent beginner-friendly recommended layouts—are equally mandatory.

